---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const outcomes = [
  { metric: '60%', label: 'improvement in response and recovery metrics through clearer operating practices' },
  { metric: '3', label: 'combined businesses aligned to shared operating practices' },
  { metric: '1', label: 'India-based team onboarded into the shared operating model' },
];

const operatingModel = [
  {
    number: '01',
    title: 'Clarify the signal',
    body: 'Improve alerting and escalation inputs so teams can distinguish actionable customer-impacting work from noise and know when ownership should change.'
  },
  {
    number: '02',
    title: 'Define ownership',
    body: 'Create clearer response paths, responsibilities, documentation, and governance so work does not stall between technical and customer-facing teams.'
  },
  {
    number: '03',
    title: 'Standardize the practice',
    body: 'Turn effective response and readiness behaviors into repeatable operating practices that can be used consistently across combined organizations.'
  },
  {
    number: '04',
    title: 'Enable the team',
    body: 'Support adoption through documentation, shared expectations, onboarding, and cross-team coordination so the operating model works beyond the people who created it.'
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Program Delivery & Operating Model | Mike Gilmore"
  description="A public-safe case study of program delivery, response ownership, operating-model standardization, governance, and team enablement."
>
  <header class="case-hero shell">
    <div class="case-hero__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case study · Program delivery & operating model</p>
      <h1>Making response ownership and operating practices easier to follow across teams.</h1>
      <p>
        Some reliability and delivery problems are not caused by a missing tool. They come from unclear ownership,
        inconsistent escalation paths, fragmented documentation, or teams using different operating expectations.
      </p>
      <p class="case-note">Public-safe summary based on substantiated professional experience. Internal procedures, organization details, and private operational artifacts are intentionally excluded.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="case-hero__role" aria-label="Role and focus">
      <p class="signal-label">Role pattern</p>
      <p>Program delivery with technical operations context</p>
      <p class="signal-label">Focus</p>
      <p>Ownership · governance · standardization · team enablement</p>
    </aside>
  </header>

  <section class="case-outcomes" aria-labelledby="operating-outcomes-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="case-section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Evidence</p>
        <h2 id="operating-outcomes-heading">The operating system around the work became part of the solution.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="case-metric-grid">
        {outcomes.map((outcome) => (
          <div class="case-metric">
            <strong>{outcome.metric}</strong>
            <span>{outcome.label}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell case-story" aria-labelledby="operating-context-heading">
    <aside class="case-story__rail">
      <p class="eyebrow">Context</p>
      <p>Combined technical organizations</p>
      <p>Customer-facing operations</p>
      <p>Cross-team adoption and onboarding</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="case-story__body">
      <h2 id="operating-context-heading">When ownership is ambiguous, technical problems become coordination problems.</h2>
      <p>
        Response quality depends on more than technical skill. Teams also need clear escalation paths, useful alerts,
        documented expectations, and a common understanding of who owns the next decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        As organizations and teams were brought together, the work included standardizing those practices so response,
        readiness, and follow-through did not depend on tribal knowledge or a single group’s habits.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft" aria-labelledby="operating-model-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="case-section-heading case-section-heading--dark">
        <p class="eyebrow">Operating model</p>
        <h2 id="operating-model-heading">Turn good response behavior into a repeatable system.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="case-flow">
        {operatingModel.map((step) => (
          <li>
            <span class="case-flow__number">{step.number}</span>
            <h3>{step.title}</h3>
            <p>{step.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell case-story" aria-labelledby="operating-analysis-heading">
    <aside class="case-story__rail">
      <p class="eyebrow">What this demonstrates</p>
      <p>Program delivery</p>
      <p>Process improvement</p>
      <p>Change management</p>
      <p>Documentation & governance</p>
      <p>Operational analysis</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="case-story__body">
      <h2 id="operating-analysis-heading">The work sits between systems analysis, change management, and technical operations.</h2>
      <p>
        The technical environment supplied the constraints, but the improvement work depended on understanding handoffs,
        identifying where process and ownership broke down, documenting the target behavior, and helping teams adopt a shared model.
      </p>
      <p>
        Those practices contributed to a 60% improvement in response and recovery metrics while supporting standardization
        across three combined businesses and onboarding an India-based team into the shared operating approach.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark" aria-labelledby="operating-takeaway-heading">
    <div class="shell case-takeaway">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Takeaway</p>
      <h2 id="operating-takeaway-heading">Better delivery often comes from making ownership, expectations, and handoffs explicit.</h2>
      <p>
        The pattern I carry forward is to treat operating practices as part of the product experience: make the signal clearer,
        define who owns the next action, document the shared process, and build adoption into the change itself.
      </p>
      <a class="button button--secondary case-button-light" href="/work/">Back to selected work</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
